    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling leverage, anchored by **Josh Naylor** (64.20) and **James Wood** (62.98). **Josh Naylor** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Ryne Nelson; his projected output is bolstered by an ideal #3 hole placement and a +5% bump from his dynamic platoon split. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains our premier offensive threat; despite facing a respectable Michael King, **James Wood** benefits from a park factor boost and the optimal leadoff spot, making him a cornerstone play despite the inherent risk of facing a high-strikeout arm. We are also leaning heavily on **Vinnie Pasquantino** (66.81) and **Brice Turang** (60.94), both of whom take advantage of sub-par opposing starters to push our daily efficiency into the strong tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros**, who posted a 53.93 score\u2014a mark that would have comfortably started on a lighter day. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from an excellent park factor and a weak matchup against Adrian Houser, the optimizer ultimately favored the stability of **Seiya Suzuki** (51.21) and the specialized utility value of **Zach McKinstry** (57.58), who offers a surprising +18% bump due to the SP skill profile of Anthony Kay. We are maintaining caution regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status; specifically, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Travis Bazzana** face tough tests against Bryan Woo and Sonny Gray, respectively, with low SP_xERA values threatening to drag their floor below the 50-point threshold. Monitor the weather in Seattle and ensure **Jose Caballero** remains in the order, as his utility score is highly sensitive to his slotting in the nine-hole.",
